<title>NEW ZEALAND: Reserve Bank of NZ changes some management jobs.</title>
<headline>Reserve Bank of NZ changes some management jobs.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of New Zealand on Wednesday said it had appointed Ken Sullivan as chief manager of corporate services.</p>
<p>He was previously manager of accounting services. That job was taken by Steve Anderson, previously chief manager of the registry department.</p>
<p>John Woodhouse, previously manager of corporate services, will take on Anderson's old job.</p>
<p>Deputy Governor Dick Lang said the transfers were designed to widen the experience of those involved.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
